[38;5;231m⏺[39m Added the checkbox to [38;5;153mindex.html:8-40[39m.

  The pattern for one task item:

  [90m<[34mli[90m [36mclass[90m=[31m"task"[90m>[39m
    [90m<[34minput[90m [36mtype[90m=[31m"checkbox"[90m [36mid[90m=[31m"task-1"[90m>[39m
    [90m<[34mlabel[90m [36mclass[90m=[31m"task__label"[90m [36mfor[90m=[31m"task-1"[90m>[39mTask text[90m</[34mlabel[90m>[39m
  [90m</[34mli[90m>[39m

  Notes on what I chose:

  - [1mNative [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">[0m rather than a custom widget — the on/off state lives in the element, so keyboard
    support, focus, and screen-reader semantics come free.
  - [1mNo JavaScript.[0m The done state renders via the [38;5;153m:checked + .task__label[39m CSS sibling selector. State is not persisted
    across reloads; say the word if you want it saved to [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m.
  - [1mTwo sample items[0m so the page isn't empty. Replace them with real tasks; each needs a unique [38;5;153mid[39m matching its label's
    [38;5;153mfor[39m.

  No tests exist in this repo, so nothing was run beyond loading the markup mentally — the change is markup and CSS
  only.

